\pard\sa80\fs22 Executes PowerShell scripts locally by spawning a new PowerShell process with configurable timeout, execution policy, and output capture. Useful for isolating script execution or running scripts in a fresh PowerShell context. Prefers {\f1 pwsh\f0} (PowerShell 7+) on all platforms and falls back to {\f1 powershell.exe\f0} (Windows PowerShell 5.1) only when {\f1 pwsh\f0} is not available. Returns a hashtable with success status and combined output.\par
